From: pmOS Q706F fixes
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250-lenovo-q706f: disable unused PCIe2 and PM8009 PON

Android DTBO for board-id 0x30d08 sets both pcie1 and pcie2 to disabled.
Mainline left pcie2 okay, so the RC probes, prints dummy vdda supplies,
then "Device not found".

pm8009's pon@800 also probes as "qcom-pon" and collides with PM8150 PON
(-EEXIST). Disable it; power/volume keys stay on PM8150.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
@@ -951,14 +951,18 @@
 	};
 };
 
 &pcie2 {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &pcie2_phy {
 	vdda-phy-supply = <&vreg_l5a_0p88>;
 	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l9a_1p2>;
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&pm8009_pon {
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &pm8150b_adc {
